]Unless your Supply Management organization takes it to the next level, your company is facing a 9% drop[ in] corporate profits this year due to rising prices and other[ inflation]ary pressure according to a recent Hackett Group study.[ For] a typical Global 1000 company with 27.8 billion in revenue, Hackett’s study estimated that commodity and offshore labor[ inflation] will drive a 150 million per year hit[ to] the[ bottom] line. Ouch!
